# Docker build context exclusions (Task 15).
#
# IMPORTANT: `next build` with `output: "standalone"` copies any present
# `.env*` file VERBATIM into `.next/standalone/.env` (confirmed empirically —
# see Dockerfile's build-stage comment). If `.env` (real ESPN cookies,
# SESSION_SECRET, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) were present in the build context, it
# would get baked into an image layer. Excluding it here means the build
# stage's `next build` never sees an `.env` file to copy in the first place —
# real secrets only ever reach the containers at RUNTIME, via docker-compose's
# `env_file: .env` (a bind of the host file, never an image layer).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Never ship the real database, backups, or any local data into an image —
# these are runtime volume contents (`./data:/data`), not build inputs.
data/

# Local-only / not needed for a container build.
node_modules/
.next/
.git/
.superpowers/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/

# Editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
